A nice idea. How about somehow using a lamp-post as a quest artifact?
IIRC, there was a lamppost on the Narnia side of the wardrobe portal
that was was "grown" like a tree from a bit of a lamppost brought back
by the White Witch.

Maybe the quest artifact could be a lantern which, when invoked,
creates a lamppost . The lamp can then create a portal to any existing
lamppost, allowing a fine-tuned Eye-style levelport ability. The
lantern and lampposts would also act as permanent light sources,
naturally.

Some kind of nerfing would need to be implemented to prevent making
the ascension run too easy. An easy fix would be to say that the
amulet of Yendot cannot go through portals. If further nerfing is
required, make it so that only a certain number of lampposts can exist
at once: When you create a lampost beyond that limit, the earliest
existing one disappears, or maybe just loses its portal ability (but
remains as a landmark and light source).

Alternatiely, have one single portal lamppost on the quest end level,
make that level a really safe and comfortable and useful place to have
your stash (once you've killed the witch, anyway). Then make the quest
artifact an artifact portal warddrobe that you can lug around the
dungeon... IIRC the wardrobe linked to the lamppost because it was
made of Narnian wood or something, so maybe the quest artifact could
be some other, more portable item made of Narnian wood..?

Of course, an artifact wardrobe just begs the implementation of the
armoire of invincibility...


